From 2f82c154b141749049857dbc97aeb9597260c798 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Release Prep <deploy@local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 07:38:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: swap /api to per-teacher auth, add ownership check
 (ADR-008 PR17)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- server.js: /api mount now uses requireTeacherAuth + apiLimiter
  instead of requireAdminSecret + adminLimiter. /admin/stats and
  /admin/grant-pro are untouched.
- utils/teacherAuth.js: add apiLimiter (100 req/15min), sized for
  per-teacher traffic rather than adminLimiter's 5 req/15min shared-
  secret budget.
- utils/validateEnv.js: TEACHER_JWT_SECRET is now required at startup.
- routes/api.js: enforce ownership — learner.phoneHash is compared
  against req.teacher.phoneHash before returning plan data; a mismatch
  returns the same 404 as an unknown learner (no existence oracle).
  Per ADR-008 §5.1, no service signature changed and no service became
  auth-aware.
- Tests: teacherAuth.test.js export-surface assertion updated for
  apiLimiter; api-intervention-plan.test.js req mocks now carry
  req.teacher and a new ownership section (cross-teacher -> 404,
  owner -> 200); new pr17-api-teacher-auth-wiring.test.js (source-
  inspection, matching the routing-order-*.test.js convention) locks
  down the mount swap, /admin/* staying on requireAdminSecret, the
  TEACHER_JWT_SECRET startup check, and the ADR-008 SS5.1 invariant
  that no services/flows/core module imports jsonwebtoken or reads
  the Authorization header.
- Docs: TEACHER_JWT_SECRET documented in .env.example, render.yaml,
  DEPLOY.md.

Full suite: 66/79 passing locally; remaining 13 failures are the
pre-existing sandbox-only better-sqlite3 native-binary mismatch,
unrelated to this change (none touch auth/api/admin).
